        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Show your Tin Cup Spirit – Register to Run and Donate!</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/47026.webp" alt="Show your Tin Cup Spirit – Register to Run and Donate!" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>The Community Foundation of Teton Valley is thrilled to invite you to the 17<sup>th</sup> Annual Tin Cup Challenge Event Day, on Saturday, July 20<sup>th</sup> at the Driggs City Park. Prepare yourself for a day filled with joy and camaraderie as we come together to honor our hard-working nonprofits, the incredible generosity of our community, and the spirit of philanthropy. </p>

<p>Jumpstart your day by running in support of local nonprofits! Competitive 5K and 10K runners will kick off the action at 9:00 AM, followed by Fun Run/Walkers at 9:03 AM on Ashely Street. Registering in advance? Great news! Fun Run/Walkers sign up for free. However, if you wait to join us on Event Day, there will be a nominal fee of $10. Please note that only competitive entrants will be timed and that registration fees increase at 5 PM on Friday, July 19, 2023. Register&nbsp;online, at the Community Foundation booth at the Driggs Farmers Market on Fridays from 9 AM – 1 PM, or between 7:30 AM &#8211; 8:30 AM at the Race Registration pavilion on Event Day. Pick up your complimentary T-shirt at the Foundation office, the Farmers Market, or on Event Day &#8211; while supplies last.</p>

<p>But that&#8217;s not all! Prepare to immerse yourself in an array of exciting activities and entertainment. After the run, treat yourself to a well-deserved FREE breakfast before exploring the critical missions of over 50 nonprofit booths until noon. Discover more about their impactful work while enjoying various festivities, including the Diaper Derby, folkloric dancing, soap hockey, and the chance to experience a flight simulator. If that isn&#8217;t enough, we also have a special treat for animal lovers. Visit our delightful menagerie of horses, mules, mini-horses, dogs, and puppies &#8211; ready to bring joy to your day.</p>

<p>In the spirit of the Tin Cup Challenge, we invite you to show your support and enthusiasm by dressing for success alongside your favorite nonprofit. By doing so, your organization will have a chance to win the prestigious Tin Cup Spirit Award, with a grand prize of $200 for first place, $100 for second place, and $75 for third place. Stay tuned as the event stage comes alive at 10:30 AM to announce the Dawn Banks Award, Spirit Awards, and Race Awards recipients. </p>

<p>Join us, the Community Foundation of Teton Valley, in acknowledging the profound impact of local nonprofits by participating in the 17<sup>th</sup> Annual Tin Cup Challenge on Saturday, July 20<sup>th</sup>. Remember that together, as a community, we can make a difference. If you wish to go the extra mile, consider donating cash, a check, stocks, or online at www.TinCupChallenge.com during the Giving Period. Generous Business &amp; Community Challengers partially match donations received before Friday, July 26 at 5 PM. </p>

<a href="https://www.raceentry.com/races/15th-annual-tin-cup-challenge/2024/register" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Register to Run</a>

<a href="https://cfjh.iphiview.com/cfjh/DonateNow/Results/tabid/461/dispatch/givingopportunities_geo$1/Default.aspx#dispatch=GivingOpportunities_geo%241" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Donate</a>

<p>For more information, we encourage you to visit the Community Foundation&#8217;s website, call us at 208.354.0230, email via info@cftetonvalley.org, visit our booth at the Farmers Market, or stop by our office. We can&#8217;t wait to see you there! </p>
